More real life code: My current favorite is Sim. Here is the summary
Scott Schwartz posted sometime ago:

| Sim is a program by Xiaoqiu Huang and Webb Miller that computes the
| $n$ best local alignments and corresponding similarity scores given
| two sequences of DNA.  On the data below (5K base pairs of tobacco and
| liverwort), it takes about half an hour to run on a SparcStation.  
| 
| As a benchmark, Sim has some interesting features.  First, it is a real
| application, not a synthetic benchmark by any means.  This code is in
| daily use by real biologists at NIH and elsewhere, although they
| generally run it on longer sequences.  Second, we've seen that vendors
| like to tune their compilers, at least partly, based on what popular
| benchmarks show.  Sun's new compiler doesn't seem to do a better job
| optimizing Sim than the old one yet.  Third, since it runs for a
| reasonable amount of time, you can see how the system reacts to a
| (more) typical workload.  Finally, it doesn't make heavy use of
| libraries (only a bit of stdio and a touch of malloc), so library code
| quality and static/dynamic linking isn't a factor.  The code is all
| integer.

Here are the results. I added the dec3000/400 and RS6000-M550
results.

# sim 8 tob.38-44 liv.42-48

dec3000/400	  525.7 real     517.4 user     0.4 sys (cc -O2)
hp720		  573.8 real	 571.3 user	0.1 sys         
RS6000-M550       954.8 real     474.8 user     0.0 sys
ibm3090		 1896.8 real	 811.6 user	6.4 sys	(wrong answer)
ibm6000		 2940.6 real	 837.6 user	0.0 sys
ss2		 1337.2 real	1334.7 user	0.6 sys (cc -O4)
ss2		 2448.0 real	1347.0 user	0.6 sys (SC1.0 -fast -O4)
ss2		 2552.6 real	1406.1 user	1.3 sys (SC1.0 -fast -O2)
ss2		 1431.4 real	1417.4 user	1.1 sys (cc -O2)
next		 1863.3 real	1842.2 user	7.5 sys  
SGI		 1975.1 real	1972.4 user	0.3 sys
ss1+		 2246.3 real	2234.7 user	1.4 sys  
fx/80		10226.1 real	7584.0 user	0.5 sys
sun3/50		12661.5 real   11283.9 user    82.5 sys (gcc -O)
ps2/70 	           --		--		--

I do not know if anyone else has compiled more results. I placed the
bundled source for this benchmark on nexus.yorku.ca:pub/oz/sim.shar.Z

hope someone posts the results for HP9000/735.

oz
