broadley@neurocog.lrdc.pitt.edu (Bill Broadley) writes:

> I'm trying to take a DAT tape written on a ALPHA OSF/1 1.2, and get it to
> a hp-735 HPUX 9.01.
> 
I'm right in the middle of a DAT tape transfer from Prime Computer
to HP 9000/8xx @ 9.01.  What works in our case is to use "dd"
as follows:

dd if=/dev/rmt/0mn ibs=16k obs=16k of=f1

The first "file" loaded is the tape header and can be discarded.
The "no-rewind" device file positions the tape to the next "file"
which is the real data.

We have a program that interprets Prime's MAGSAV format and loads
it to our target database, but dd is pretty generic in terms of
just getting the stuff off tape and onto disk.  What you do with
it then is up to you.

Regards,
