CAP might not run on OSF V1.2, because V1.2 does not support the
"packet filter" facility.  (It's possible that CAP could be made
to run using the DLI facility, which apparently is available in
V1.2.  I don't know of anyone who has tried to do this.)

I'm probably not authorized to talk about future product plans, so
I can't say something like "a future release of OSF will support
the packet filter".  On the other hand, I managed to find a few
CAP users who were willing to field-test an OSF kernel (not yet
a product!) and who managed to get CAP running on it.  We found
and fixed a few kernel bugs like this, and we don't know of any
remaining bugs.

I imagine that when (oops, I mean "if") a version of OSF ships
that includes packet filter support, a modified version of CAP
should be available shortly thereafter.  But not from me, I don't
run CAP myself.

Your Digital sales representative might be able to tell you when
the next release of OSF will ship.

-Jeff


