Yes :-)

Paragon OSF/1 Release 1.0.1 Server 1.0 R1.0; Mon Apr 19 13:37:28 PDT 1993;
bash$ uname -a
Paragon OSF/1 paragon 1.0.1 R1.0 paragon

The biggest problem is making the bash-Makefile. It wants a "good"
old cpp, and the CPP860 provided doesn't cut it.  (How they got X
to compile, I don't know, but I guess they just compiled a BSD
version of cpp for that).  Provided you compile your own cpp (BSD
or GNU), or do that processing on another machine, things are
quite smooth.  (Another option is cross-compiling using ICC860
from a normal UNIX machine - this also works well).

I compiled when running an alpha version of the operating system,
so my patches may not be very optimal, but they still worked when
compiling today.

  Good luck,

Arne H. Juul  (arnej@lise.unit.no)
