Glen,

The Digital techie may have been referring to the Digital Extended Math Library for DEC OSF/1 AXP...

"The Digital Extended Math Library (DXML) V2.0 is a set of libraries of 
mathematical subroutines that are optimized for Digital platforms. Four 
libraries are included covering the areas of Basic Linear Algebra (BLAS), 
Linear System and Eigenproblem Solvers, Sparse Linear System Solvers, and 
Signal Processing.

"Unlike third-party math libraries such as those from IMSL and NAG, DXML V2.0 
is optimized for the underlying architecture, and is ideal for production codes and benchmark situations where performance is important.

"DXML V2.0 includes LAPACK, a library of linear and eigenproblem solvers 
developed by a consortium of industry and government laboratories. LAPACK solvers employ the latest blocked algorithms that perform better on modern computer architectures using virtual memory, caches, and register files.  
LAPACK will supersede LINPACK and EISPACK for most users.

"A Sparse Linear System Solver library is included, providing a selection of iterative solvers and preconditioners.  The Signal Processing library now provides a complete selection of 1-D, 2-D, 3-D and group FFTs, digital filters, convolution and correlation."

I don't know if this math library is used in performance measurement, but you 
may want to consider it.  It is packaged in a developers kit and a run-time 
kit.  It has been shipping since March 93.  To get the real nuts & bolts, look at the SPD:

	gatekeeper.dec.com: /pub/DEC/DECinfo/SPD/41-84-00.txt

Hope this helps,

