My mailserver is a DEC RISC system running Ultrix.  I regularly read
mail there and (NFS mounted) from a Sun SPARCstation.  I just built
Elm 2.4p22 on a DEC Alpha machine running OSF/1.  When I invoke elm
and look at my aliases on the Alpha, I see 0 aliases (there should be
19).  If I rebuild the hashed database from aliases.text on the Alpha,
the aliases are all there on the Alpha, but when viewed from Ultrix or
SPARC boxes, I see 0 aliases.

I assume the problem here is that ndbm databases are not portable
across 32/64 bit formats.  Could the next patch to elm include code
that, if elm tries to read an alias database file and comes up with 0
entries, it will then try to parse the aliases.text file and use that
