Benchmarks on the CHARMM program (molecular modeling; energy minimization,
dynamics, vibrational modes, etc.) gave similar results; straightforward
compilation of the Unix variant produced code which completed in about 5/8
the time.  The problem size was large enough to require paging except on
machines with large amounts ( >= 128 MB perhaps? ) of RAM.  This was for a 730
vs. a 500; adjusting the results for the faster clocks of 735 vs. 500X does
not favor the Alpha.  The code is about 80,000 lines of Fortran, with a few
C calls to access system routines, and has been under active development for
around 10 years, so it is certainly not 'dusty deck' Fortran.



