We had a similar problem, and upgrading memory to 64Meg has cured the problem
to some extent. Perhaps you can persuade your local DEC rep to allow you to
try this out if you're wary of spending money on something that may not work.
I think the compilers seem to use vast amounts of memory and hence really do
cause major swapping.

> Anybody using DBX ? Can someone tell me how to get a traceback to source
> code AFTER the core file has been dumped ? On ultrix, it was just
> dbx my_prog  core

You could try using the 'use' command to specify where the sources are kept.
It defaults to '.' I believe. Also, there is another debugger called ladbx on
our system. It can handle some things dbx cannot, but is in general far more
susceptible to crashing itself.

> OS/F gives my 'source code not available' no matter what f77 options I try.
> Speaking of F77 options, is there  an otion such as -fpe3. The man pages
